WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.118 --> 00:00:02.969
-My first guest
is an Emmy-nominated actress

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:05.004
and a judge on
"America's Got Talent."

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:09.041
The new season premieres June
1st at 8:00 p.m. here on NBC.

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:11.978
Here's Sofia Vergara!

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.614
Sofia! Welcome back!

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.982
-How are you?

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.917
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.819
I am great.
It is so great to see you.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.621
Thank you so much
for coming back on the show.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.089
-No, thank you for having me.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:26.092
I'm still here in the same place
where you saw me last.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.693
-Yeah.
-In the basement of my house.

00:00:27.693 --> 00:00:29.295
-Your husband, Joe Manganiello,

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.831
was nice enough to come
on our show not too long ago

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.634
and introduced me
to a new family member,

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.670
which I totally love --
-Who?

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.305
-He stole the show -- Bubbles.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.241
-Oh, oh, yeah.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.543
-Now, look at this.
-Yeah.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:44.610
-Unbelievable.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.412
-Yeah, that's Bubbles.

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:47.680
She hates me.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.382
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.050
-What do you mean, Bubbles --
-She hates me.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.019
-She does not like you? Bubbles?
I thought --

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.553
-No, no. I mean --

00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:56.989
-I thought this was your dog.
-She was supposed to be for me.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.658
-Yes.
-She was supposed to be my dog.

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:00.827
-Yes.
-And she arrived to the house.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:04.396
And she -- I don't know. She
thought that she was for Joe,

00:01:04.396 --> 00:01:05.864
and that's all she wants to do.

00:01:05.864 --> 00:01:08.201
She's, like, you know,
after him all day long,

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.870
harassing him.
-[ Chuckles ] "Harassing him."

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.706
-It's an obsession
this dog has with him.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.308
It's like -- It's horrific.

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.576
She hates me. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.576 --> 00:01:19.045
-[ Laughs ] Horrific.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.114
You actually -- But you were --
-Yes. Horrific.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.749
She's super mean to me.

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:25.250
She bites me.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.020
-This is mean to you?

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.154
-Yes, yes.
-She's so cute!

00:01:29.154 --> 00:01:32.024
-But she's not.
She's not that cute in person.

00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:33.426
She's old.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.828
She looks like a baby,
but she's like 8 years old,

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.396
so it's like 69.

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:39.198
So she's like
a lot older than me.

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:40.366
I'm 49.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.934
-Sofia, you were trying
to be nice to her.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:45.271
You actually, on Joe's birthday,
you made him --

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.772
This is an amazing work of art.

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:49.141
A Bubbles birthday cake.

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:51.844
-Well, yeah, 'cause I wanted
to make him happy.

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:53.046
[ Audience awws ]

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.047
-And that's so --
-I wanted to make him happy,

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:57.783
because, you know,
that's like -- that's his baby.

00:01:57.783 --> 00:02:01.253
He -- Well, I have to say,
he treats her like she's a --

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:02.889
you know, a little
puppy baby dog,

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:04.657
like a little daughter he has?

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:08.061
But she insists of, you know,
like, behaving like a concubine

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.296
or like beast friends
or something.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.332
It's like, she sleeps with him.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:14.233
-Oh, my --
-She gets angry

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:16.402
when I walk in the room.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.938
I mean, it's a whole thing now
in the house.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.240
-She's almost making
an expression here, like,

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.111
I like the cake but I know that
you had something to do with it.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:27.647
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.681
Very interesting.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:32.118
-I'm telling you she hates me.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:34.587
-You guys are a great couple.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.555
Now you've been married
for five years.

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:40.059
You do not have the same taste
in music, though.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.160
-No, no, no, no.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.096
I mean, sometimes yes.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:45.798
But usually -- Usually, no.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:51.371
Joe is a little more
out there than me.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:54.740
You know, I just like
simple Latin music.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.643
-No, but he loves metal, right?

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.845
He loves -- He's a metal head.

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.781
-Yeah. It's like music

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:04.183
that is coming
out of the devil's house.

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:05.718
-No, no, that is not --
-It's horrific.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:08.121
-No, that's not
a way to describe --

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:10.589
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:13.392
-It's like sometimes he puts it,
like, when we're in the car,

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:14.927
and it takes me, like,
some minutes

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:18.030
to realize why I'm having,
like, palpitations,

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.165
why I'm not feeling good.
I think -- I feel like

00:03:20.165 --> 00:03:22.235
I am having, like, high blood
pressure or something.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.270
And it's like, "God,
it's the stupid music

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.871
that is such --"

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:28.741
How can you drive
with this intensity?

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.609
-Yeah. Between that and Bubbles,

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:32.945
I don't know how
you're doing all this.

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:34.981
-No, believe me. I don't know.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.548
You know, and the pandemic,

00:03:36.548 --> 00:03:39.252
I was, you know, inside
this house with the two of them.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.620
I mean, it was not fun.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.489
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:45.758
-I will say, though, by the way,

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.993
thank goodness you're on
"America's Got Talent."

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:49.762
You're fantastic on there.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:53.432
And it was a crazy season
last season,

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:56.335
because Heidi got sick, right?

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:57.770
-Heidi got sick.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.005
Simon got in
a horrific accident.

00:04:00.005 --> 00:04:01.440
Like, he couldn't walk.
-Yeah.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.642
-And it was, like,
a whole ordeal.

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:05.911
The pandemic happened.

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:07.747
-But you stepped up.
-You know, like --

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.815
-You stepped up,
and you were there.

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:11.451
-I loved it.
-Yes.

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:13.018
I was great.

00:04:13.018 --> 00:04:16.055
-No, no, that's --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:19.892
That's not -- Yes.
That's not -- You were --

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.660
That's not really what --
I did mean that.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.529
But I think you're good,

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.264
and we talked about this
last time you were on the show.

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:27.833
As a judge,
you are a good judge.

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:30.169
And I said, "Is it difficult?"

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:33.039
Because it's hard to let people
down if you don't like their --

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:35.774
-It's difficult.
-Their talent, yeah.

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:37.043
Yeah.
-It's hard, you know?

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:39.578
You want to be fair.
You realize, you know,

00:04:39.578 --> 00:04:42.381
that this is, like, the moment

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:44.517
that can change
somebody else's life.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.218
So you have to
take it seriously.

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:49.322
They can change their families'
life, their life.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.923
So you want to be fair.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.592
There's so many talent
out there.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:55.594
There's so many also
horrific thing that shows up

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:58.798
in the stage that you're like,
"Why? Why are you here?"

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.434
[ Laughter ]
So you want to be fair.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.602
-Yeah, you want to be fair.

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:05.004
But then last time,
you said that you have --

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:09.041
You don't like ukuleles.

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:11.077
You don't even want
to see a ukulele.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:14.646
You said, so if that comes on
the stage, you don't want it.

00:05:14.646 --> 00:05:15.815
-No, but that's nothing --

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.051
Like, I'm not going to
immediately cut them

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:19.418
because it's a "ukuleelee."

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:21.120
I'm not going to do that.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.122
It's just that I realize --
-Ukulele.

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:24.957
It's a ukulele.
-Okay.

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.058
Whatever.

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:27.927
[ Laughter ]
So it's like, I just don't

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:31.130
want to, you know, listen to a
whole concert

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:34.800
of a "ukulele-ey," I mean --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.836
-It's not a ukulele-le,
either, but --

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.404
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:39.938
-Okay, really? Really?
-I'm not sure. I'm not sure.

00:05:39.938 --> 00:05:41.640
No, I'm sorry. No, you're right.
It could be.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.109
But I don't want to --

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:45.878
I'm not sure if I would go to
a giant whole ukulele concert.

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.647
But they mix it up.

00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:49.715
I mean, now --
-Yes. No, it's great.

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:52.084
The show is great.
I mean, I love the dancers.

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:55.988
I realize that, how much I enjoy
watching people dance.

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:58.324
I mean, I guess I'm Latin.
But I didn't know --

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:00.026
I mean, it's really my favorite.

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:02.461
-It's your favorite part?
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:04.997
Here's a peek at next week's
season premiere

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:06.365
of "America's Got Talent."

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:07.967
Take a look at this.

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.902
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:13.139
♪♪

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:14.740
-He did this too many times.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.243
All his hairs left.

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:22.715
♪♪

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:24.317
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:26.285
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:29.789
♪♪

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:31.657
-I love it.

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.325
-Sofia Vergara, everybody.

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:36.395
When we come back, Sofia and I
are going head-to-head

00:06:36.395 --> 00:06:39.232
in a new game called
"Piece of Cake Trivia."

